1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,667
This is HAI, a new rule engine for Hubitat.

2
00:00:02,667 --> 00:00:11,784
You can write rules yourself, describe them to the AI, see exactly what they'll do before they run, and move your Rule Machine rules across safely.

3
00:00:11,784 --> 00:00:12,900
Let's take a look.

4
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:18,498
Rules are built from triggers, conditions and actions, and every step reads as a sentence.

5
00:00:18,498 --> 00:00:25,506
When Porch Door opens, if it's between sunset and sunrise, turn Entry Light on, wait five minutes, then turn it off.

6
00:00:25,506 --> 00:00:27,500
No settings pages to dig through.

7
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:29,620
HAI checks the rule as you build it.

8
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:33,580
Leave a step incomplete, and it tells you straight away, in plain words.

9
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,382
Rules can do real work, too.

10
00:00:35,382 --> 00:00:46,525
This one keeps a count of entry visits in a variable, and works out the light level from the room's brightness: one hundred, minus the light reading divided by five, never below ten percent.

11
00:00:46,525 --> 00:00:51,158
And you can use everyday words: if it's dark or raining, go to full brightness.

12
00:00:51,158 --> 00:00:55,850
Variables, calculations and plain-English conditions, all readable in one place.

13
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,804
Before anything touches a real device, you can simulate the rule.

14
00:00:59,804 --> 00:01:04,536
Here's the door opening: the light comes on, and five minutes later it goes off.

15
00:01:04,536 --> 00:01:07,730
Every step is shown, with the reason it ran or didn't.

16
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,006
Or just describe it.

17
00:01:09,006 --> 00:01:12,686
The AI Rule Assistant drafts the rule using your own devices.

18
00:01:12,686 --> 00:01:15,340
It's optional, and uses your own Claude key.

19
00:01:15,370 --> 00:01:21,270
The draft goes through the same checks and the same simulator, so nothing runs until you've seen it and saved it.

20
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:23,607
Each rule runs as its own app on the hub.

21
00:01:23,607 --> 00:01:26,554
It goes on stopped, and you start it when you're ready.

22
00:01:26,554 --> 00:01:30,090
Every run is recorded, so if a rule didn't fire, it tells you why.

23
00:01:30,170 --> 00:01:34,958
Your rules are backed up every night, and you can restore one rule, or all of them.

24
00:01:34,958 --> 00:01:42,110
Automation Map shows your HAI and Rule Machine rules side by side: what they watch, what they control, and how they connect.

25
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:43,852
Already using Rule Machine?

26
00:01:43,852 --> 00:01:49,180
HAI Migration copies your rules across, and it covers every Rule Machine capability.

27
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:51,014
Each copy runs in shadow mode.

28
00:01:51,014 --> 00:02:00,110
It's switched off and changes nothing, but every time the rule fires, HAI works out what it would have done, and compares that with what Rule Machine actually did.

29
00:02:00,210 --> 00:02:01,974
When it matches, promote it.

30
00:02:01,974 --> 00:02:04,682
Rule Machine is paused, and HAI takes over.

31
00:02:04,682 --> 00:02:05,815
Changed your mind?

32
00:02:05,815 --> 00:02:07,390
Switch back in one click.

33
00:02:07,530 --> 00:02:08,710
HAI is in preview.

34
00:02:08,710 --> 00:02:11,595
Install it through HPM, from the link below.

35
00:02:11,595 --> 00:02:13,890
Try it, and tell us what you think.
